From 84cf01dd97037bf369684a193173c65f70507f5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Super User <root@localhost.localdomain>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 09:37:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: arm64: Fix HDBSS DBM incorrectly applied to VFIO MMIO
 regions

Bug Description:
HDBSS incorrectly adds DBM (Dirty Bit Modifier) to VFIO MMIO BAR regions,
causing device access issues and migration failures.

Root Cause:
In user_mem_abort(), the DBM setting logic does not check if the fault
is for device/MMIO memory. This causes VFIO MMIO BAR Stage-2 PTEs to
get DBM bit, and HDBSS hardware attempts dirty tracking on MMIO regions.

Since MMIO is not real memory, this leads to:
- Undefined hardware behavior
- Device state inconsistency
- Migration verification failures on PCI config space hardware bits

Fix:
Add !device check before setting DBM, ensuring DBM is only used for
RAM memory, not for Device/MMIO memory.

Tested:
- Two-round VFIO migration with hisi_zip accelerator
- Before fix: Second migration fails with PCI config mismatch
- After fix: All migrations succeed

Signed-off-by: HDBSS Team <hdbss@example.com>
---
 arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
index fbc62b27adc8..b505936a2f64 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
@@ -1679,7 +1679,7 @@ static int user_mem_abort(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, phys_addr_t fault_ipa,
 		prot |= KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_W;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_HDBSS
-	if (kvm->enable_hdbss && logging_active)
+	if (!device && kvm->enable_hdbss && logging_active)
 		prot |= KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_DBM;
 #endif
 
